\image(figures/bron_kerbosch.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Frame four has R=[2,1], P empty and X=[0]. It reports nothing because zero extends that pair. The returned triangle [0,1,2] was discovered earlier along R=[2,0,1]. The histogram is calculated in the core from emitted cliques.)
\alttext(Three green bars of height one occur at clique sizes two, three and four. The chart counts every maximal clique, rather than keeping only the largest.)

At the root, pivot two has five neighbours in P, so only vertices two and six
are branch candidates. Inside R=[2], the pivot is three. Its branch snapshot
is [0,1,3]. After processing zero, the parent moves zero into X. Selecting one
then produces the non-reporting R=[2,1] frame. The search visits ten frames
and reports three cliques. No second search or reconstructed tree supplies
the records or counters.

> A controlled family with exponentially many answers

Partition 3q vertices into q groups of three. The native complete-multipartite
generator joins every pair from different groups and no pair within a group.
A maximal clique must choose exactly one vertex from every group: two from
one group are not adjacent, while omitting a group leaves a possible extension.
There are therefore K=3^q distinct maximal cliques, each containing q vertices.
The same argument gives a product of part sizes for unequal positive groups.

For these equal groups, every pivot leaves the three vertices of its group
as branch candidates. Earlier siblings from that group are non-neighbours of
the next choice and disappear from the child's X. Hence the call tree has
three children per internal frame and depth q:

$$
C_0=1,\qquad C_q=1+3C_{q-1}
 =\frac{3^{q+1}-1}{2}.
$$

The programme checks both formulas against native counts. These are logical
calls and materialised answers, not timings. With zero groups the existing
API convention returns one empty clique; the table includes that control.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bron_kerbosch_output_growth.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> vertices,cliques,calls;
  std::size_t expected=1;
  std::print("| groups q | vertices | actual maximal cliques | 3^q | actual calls | (3^(q+1)-1)/2 | maximum depth |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (int q=0;q<=8;++q) {
    if (q) expected*=3;
    const auto adjacency=dm::algorithms::complete_multipartite_graph(std::vector<int>(q,3));
    const auto trace=dm::algorithms::bron_kerbosch_trace(3*q,adjacency);
    const auto expected_calls=(3*expected-1)/2;
    if (trace.cliques.size()!=expected || trace.recursive_calls!=expected_calls || trace.max_depth!=std::size_t(q)) return 1;
    vertices.push_back(3*q);cliques.push_back(trace.cliques.size());calls.push_back(trace.recursive_calls);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",q,trace.vertex_count,trace.cliques.size(),
        expected,trace.recursive_calls,expected_calls,trace.max_depth);
  }
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create().lines(vertices,cliques,"returned cliques",dm::RGB{37,99,235},2)
      .points(vertices,cliques,"",dm::RGB{37,99,235},4)
      .lines(vertices,calls,"actual calls",dm::RGB{217,119,6},2)
      .points(vertices,calls,"",dm::RGB{217,119,6},4)
      .title("Three choices per part: exponential output despite pivoting")
      .x_label("vertices in complete multipartite graph").y_label("materialised cliques or search calls")
      .y_limits(0,12500).size(900,500).save_svg("build/bron_kerbosch_output_growth.svg");
}
```
